  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock id="f-12" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;12. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInOfficersDirectorsMajorSecurityHoldersAndVotingPowersOfTheRespondentTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock id="f-13" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;13. None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfSignificantEventThatRespondentParticipatesInACashManagementProgramsTextBlock>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-14" contextRef="c-1">Equitrans, L.P.</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:RespondentLegalName id="f-15" contextRef="c-1">Equitrans, L.P.</ferc:RespondentLegalName>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-16" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;A. Description of Business&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Equitrans, L.P. (the Company) is a Pennsylvania limited partnership that owns and operates an interstate natural gas pipeline system subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) pursuant to the Natural Gas Act. As of March 31, 2026, Equitrans Investments, LLC (Equitrans Investments) held a 97.25% ownership interest in the Company, and Equitrans Services, LLC (Equitrans Services) held a 2.75% ownership interest in the Company. Equitrans Services is the Company's general partner. Both Equitrans Investments and Equitrans Services are subsidiaries of PipeBox LLC, which is a joint venture in which a wholly owned subsidiary of EQT Corporation (EQT) is a member.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;EQT's employees provide operational support and manage the Company&#8217;s daily business operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Basis of Presentation. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;These Financial Statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC as set forth in its Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP). Differences between the Financial Statements and GAAP include differences related to income taxes, purchase accounting and the classification of certain accounts in the Balance Sheets, Statements of Income and Statements of Cash Flows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Due to the seasonal nature of the Company's utility customer contracts, the results of operations for the three months ended March 31, 2026 are not necessarily indicative of the results that may be expected for the year ended December 31, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;---------&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="-sec-extract:summary;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;B. Rate and Other Regulatory Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On September 21, 2018, the Company submitted an application under Docket No. CP18-549 for its Swarts Complex Abandonment Project under Section 7(b) of the Natural Gas Act. The project consists of abandoning eighteen injection and withdrawal wells in the Swarts Complex over an approximate ten and one-half year period. On March 20, 2019, FERC issued an order granting the Company&#8217;s application to abandon the wells. The Company abandoned the first of the wells on March 21, 2019. During the third quarter of 2019, the Company recorded $0.1 million in loss on disposition of property for the abandonment of one subject well. The second Swarts Complex well was abandoned on June 17, 2020; during the first quarter of 2021, the Company recorded a $0.4 million loss on disposition of property for the abandonment of the Second Swarts Complex well. The third Swarts Complex well was abandoned on April 28, 2021. During the third quarter of 2021, the Company recorded a less than $0.1 million loss on disposition of property for abandonment of the third Swarts Complex well. Four Swarts Complex wells were abandoned during November 2021; during the second quarter of 2022, the Company recorded a $0.3 million loss on disposition for abandonment of the four Swarts wells. The Company abandoned the eighth Swarts Complex well on June 7, 2022 and recorded a $0.1 million loss on disposition of this well during the third quarter of 2022. The Company abandoned the ninth Swarts Complex well on October 31, 2022 and recorded a less than $0.1 million loss on disposal of this well during the fourth quarter of 2022. On April 12, 2022, the Company submitted an application amendment under Docket Nos. CP18-549-001 and CP22-162-000. The amended project consists of the Company proposing to plug and abandon five of the remaining wells (well numbers 603791, 603792, 603793, 603795 and 603797) and associated facilities rather than abandoning the wells by sale to CONSOL Energy LLC. The Company received its Order Approving Amendment to Abandonment Authorization on January 26, 2023. The Company completed the abandonment of well 603792 on July 6, 2023. On July 24, 2023, the Company filed a Notice of Change in Planned Abandonment and Request to Partially Vacate Authorization with FERC in which it requested to revert to abandonment by sale for wells 603791, 603793, 603795 and 603797 as authorized in the 2019 Order. Four Swarts Complex wells were abandoned on March 13, 2024, and the Company recorded a $0.1 million loss on the disposition of these wells during the second quarter of 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On June 2, 2021, the Company submitted under Docket No. CP21-455 an application to plug and abandon Well 3660 under FERC's prior notice regulations. The project consists of the plugging and abandonment of an injection and withdrawal well in the Pratt Storage Field. Protests to the Company's request were filed in that docket. FERC issued an Environmental Assessment Report on July 17, 2023, and, on October 23, 2023, FERC issued its Order authorizing abandonment. On January 29, 2026, the Company completed the plugging and abandonment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;-------&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On January 28, 2022, the Company submitted under Docket No. CP22-44 an application for its Ohio Valley Connector Expansion (OVCX) Project under Section 7(c) of the Natural Gas Act. The project consists of acquiring the Cygrymus Compressor Station and adding two turbines to the system, adding a compressor unit at the Corona Compressor Station, adding a compressor unit at the Plasma Compressor Station, constructing approximately 5.5 miles of pipeline, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;installing a deep anode groundbed and rectifier for cathodic protection and adding ancillary facilities. FERC issued the Final Environmental Impact Statement for the project on January 20, 2023, and the Company received its Certificate Authorization on June 15, 2023. On July 27, 2023, the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers issued the last outstanding approval to the project. On July 31, 2023, FERC issued the Notice to Proceed, and the Company commenced construction. The Company placed the OVCX project facilities, except for the facilities in Pennsylvania (H-327 Pipeline, H-328 Pipeline, and Cygrymus Compressor Station), in service on March 27, 2024. The Company completed and placed the remaining project facilities in service on April 4, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On June 30, 2023, the Company submitted an application under Docket No. CP23-507 for its Swarts and Hunters Cave Well Replacement Project under Sections 7(b) and 7(c) of the Natural Gas Act. The project consists of (i) abandoning by sale nineteen injection/withdrawal wells in the existing Hunters Cave Storage Field, (ii) constructing two horizontal wells: one in the Hunters Cave Storage Field and one in the Swarts Complex to replace the capacity and capabilities of the storage fields, (iii) acquiring pipelines and related equipment to serve as well lines and auxiliary facilities, and (iv) selling base gas. On December 8, 2023, FERC issued the Environmental Assessment, and the Company received its Certificate Authorization on January 31, 2024. The Company abandoned the first two wells on February 1, 2024 and three wells on April 17, 2024. The Company recorded a $0.1 million loss on the disposition of these wells during the second and third quarters of 2024. The Company abandoned one well on July 10, 2024 and four wells on July 29, 2024 and recorded a $0.2 million loss on the disposition of these wells during the third quarter of 2024. The Company abandoned two wells on October 23, 2024 and recorded a $0.1 million loss on the dispositions of these wells during the first quarter of 2025. The Hunters Cave well was completed and placed in service on December 19, 2024. The Company abandoned two wells on February 24, 2025 and recorded a $0.1 million loss on the disposition of these wells during the second quarter of 2025. In November 2025, the Company commenced construction of the Swarts Complex well and expects it to be completed during the fourth quarter of 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On September 20, 2024, the Company submitted an application in Docket No. CP23-522 to abandon a farm tap on the H-152 Pipeline under FERC's prior notice regulations due to safety concerns. On May 29, 2025, FERC issued its Order approving abandonment. The Company completed the abandonment on September 19, 2025. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On August 4, 2025, the Company submitted under Docket No. CP25-532 an application to plug and abandon Well 3629 under FERC's prior notice regulations. The project consists of the plugging and abandonment of a withdrawal well in the Pratt Storage Field. On February 20, 2026, the Company completed the plugging and abandonment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On January 21, 2026, the Company submitted under Docket No. CP26-73 an application to abandon the West Fairfield Compressor Station under FERC's prior notice regulations. The Company expects to complete the abandonment during the second quarter of 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On February 25, 2026, the Company submitted under Docket No. CP26-102 an application to abandon Unit #9 in the Comet Compressor Station under FERC's prior notice regulations. The Company expects to complete the abandonment during the second quarter of 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On May 22, 2026, the Company submitted an application to plug and abandon well 3664 under FERC's prior notice regulations. The project consists of the plugging and abandonment of an injection and withdrawal well in the Pratt Storage Field. The Company expects to complete the abandonment during the second quarter of 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;----&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;C. Related Party Transactions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;In the ordinary course of business, the Company has transactions with related parties.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;For the three months ended March 31, 2026 and 2025, the Company recognized revenues from related parties of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$90.2 million&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; and $76.5 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Employees of EQT operate the Company's assets. EQT charges the Company for the payroll and benefit costs associated with employees and carries the obligations for other employee-related benefits in EQT's financial statements. The Company is allocated a portion of EQT&#8217;s defined benefit pension plan and retiree medical life insurance liability for the retirees of the Company based on an actuarial assessment of that liability. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company incurs direct charges for certain services provided by a related party as well as allocated charges representing the Company's share of indirect charges incurred by a related party for certain costs shared by the Company and the related party. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The tables below summarize the Company's related party amounts. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:62.590%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:16.757%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:16.758%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="9" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Three Months Ended March 31,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:3pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="9" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;(Millions)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Operating and maintenance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5.6&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4.2&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Selling, general and administrative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5.8&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;6.8&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Capital expenditures&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;3.3&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;2.4&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:62.590%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:16.757%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:16.758%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;March 31, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;December 31, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style="height:3pt"&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="9" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;(Millions)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Account 146, Accounts Receivable from Associated Companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;26.2&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;29.7&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Account 234, Accounts Payable to Associated Companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;6.9&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;13.3&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;D. Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company is treated as a partnership for federal and state income tax purposes and, as such, is not subject to federal or state income taxes. Under the FERC Revised Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances, the Company records a provision for income taxes for regulatory purposes in the Financial Statements. Although the Company is not a taxable entity for income tax purposes, amounts equivalent to current and deferred income tax expense based on corporate tax rates are presented in the Financial Statements as income taxes are a cost component for the Company's currently effective rates. The Company uses the liability method of accounting for income taxes, which requires, among other things, provisions for all temporary differences between the financial and tax basis in the Company's assets and liabilities and adjustments to the existing deferred tax balances for changes in tax rates. Where deferred tax liabilities or assets will be passed through to customers in regulated rates, the Company establishes a corresponding regulatory asset or liability for the increase or decrease in future revenues that will result when the temporary differences reverse. The Company&#8217;s effective income tax rate for the three months ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ee2724;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;March 31, 2026 and 2025 was 24.6% and 24.7%, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;EQT files a consolidated federal tax return. The Company&#8217;s income taxes payable are not settled through cash with EQT. During the three months ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ee2724;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;March 31, 2026, the Company settled through equity a balance of $92.8 million, which represented income taxes payable as of December 31, 2025. During the three months ended March 31, 2025, the Company settled a balance of $65.7 million through equity, which represented income taxes payable as of December 31, 2024. The Statements of Cash Flows present the impact of such settlements as non-cash transactions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ffffff;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;---------&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;E. Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The following table summarizes changes in cash and cash equivalents during the three months ended&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ee2724;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;March 31, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:38.334%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.691%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.691%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.694%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;December 31, 2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Increase&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;March 31, 2026&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#cceeff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Account 131, Cash&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#cceeff;border-top:1pt solid #000;pad