      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Net decrease in customer storage inventory.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Storage migration losses are not reported on this page. Based on discussions with Commission staff, Page 520 does not provide a space to record storage migration losses.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Applies to entire schedule: The Company reports volumetric data based on accounting month data, which includes production month on a two month lag. For example, first quarter data includes the November and December and January production months. February and March volumetric data will be presented in the next quarterly filing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
